{"code":"it","name":"Italian","native":"Italiano","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A1","pronunciation":{"title":"Sing Italian from day one","rules":[{"rule":"Every vowel is pure and clear","explain":"A=ah, E=eh, I=ee, O=oh, U=oo. CIAO = chow. Sing each vowel fully — never swallow them!","examples":[{"t":"ciao","r":"chow","en":"hello/bye"},{"t":"amore","r":"ah-MOH-reh","en":"love"}]},{"rule":"C and G change before E/I","explain":"CA=ka but CE=che, CI=chee. GA=ga but GE=je. CH forces KA (CHIESA=kee-EH-sa), GH forces GA.","examples":[{"t":"ciao","r":"chow","en":"hello"},{"t":"gelato","r":"jeh-LAH-toh","en":"ice cream"}]},{"rule":"GLI = lyi, GN = ny","explain":"FAMIGLIA = fah-MEE-lyah (family). LASAGNA = lah-ZAHN-ya. GN hums like onion's NI!","examples":[{"t":"famiglia","r":"fah-MEE-lyah","en":"family"},{"t":"lasagne","r":"lah-ZAHN-yeh","en":"lasagne"}]},{"rule":"Double letters hold longer","explain":"PALA (shovel) vs PALLA (ball) — hold the L! ANNO (year) stretches the N. Double = longer, always.","examples":[{"t":"palla","r":"PAHL-lah","en":"ball"},{"t":"anno","r":"AHN-noh","en":"year"}]},{"rule":"Stress usually falls second-last","explain":"GRA-zie, PI-zza, GE-la-to. An accent mark forces final stress: CITTÀ (city), CAFFÈ (coffee).","examples":[{"t":"grazie","r":"GRAH-tsyeh","en":"thanks"},{"t":"città","r":"cheet-TAH","en":"city"}]}]},"alphabet":{"title":"The Italian alphabet: 21 letters","explain":"Italian uses 21 letters — J K W X Y appear only in foreign words. Learn names to spell aloud: MI CHIAMO … (my name is …), SI SCRIVE … (it is spelled …).","letters":[{"t":"a","r":"ah","tip":"as in father: AMICO"},{"t":"b","r":"bee","tip":"same as English: BENE"},{"t":"c","r":"chee","tip":"CA=ka, CE=che: CIAO"},{"t":"d","r":"dee","tip":"same as English: DOVE"},{"t":"e","r":"eh","tip":"as in bet: BENE"},{"t":"f","r":"EHf-feh","tip":"same as English: FOTO"},{"t":"g","r":"jee","tip":"GA=ga, GE=je: GELATO"},{"t":"h","r":"AHk-kah","tip":"always silent: HOTEL = oh-TEL"},{"t":"i","r":"ee","tip":"as in machine: SÌ"},{"t":"l","r":"EHL-leh","tip":"same as English: LIBRO"},{"t":"m","r":"EHM-meh","tip":"same as English: MANO"},{"t":"n","r":"EHN-neh","tip":"same as English: NOTTE"},{"t":"o","r":"oh","tip":"round O: ORO"},{"t":"p","r":"pee","tip":"same, less puff: PANE"},{"t":"q","r":"koo","tip":"always QU = kw: QUANTO"},{"t":"r","r":"EHR-reh","tip":"rolled R: ROSSO"},{"t":"s","r":"EHS-seh","tip":"S, or Z between vowels: CASA"},{"t":"t","r":"tee","tip":"same as English: TAVOLO"},{"t":"u","r":"oo","tip":"as in moon: LUNA"},{"t":"v","r":"vee","tip":"same as English: VINO"},{"t":"z","r":"DZEH-tah","tip":"dz/ts: PIZZA = PEET-tsah"},{"t":"j","r":"ee LOON-gah","tip":"foreign only: JAZZ"},{"t":"k","r":"KAHP-pah","tip":"foreign only: KARAOKE"},{"t":"w","r":"DOHP-pyah voo","tip":"foreign only: WEB"},{"t":"x","r":"eeks","tip":"foreign only: TAXI"},{"t":"y","r":"EEP-see-lohn","tip":"foreign only: YOGA"}]},"counting":{"title":"Counting 0 to 100","explain":"Learn 0–10 by heart. 11–19 glue together (undici, diciotto). 20+ joins tens + ones and DROPS a vowel: ventuno (not ventiuno!). 100 = CENTO.","numbers":[{"t":"zero","r":"DZEH-roh","en":"0"},{"t":"uno","r":"OO-noh","en":"1"},{"t":"due","r":"DOO-eh","en":"2"},{"t":"tre","r":"treh","en":"3"},{"t":"quattro","r":"KWAHT-troh","en":"4"},{"t":"cinque","r":"CHEEN-kweh","en":"5"},{"t":"sei","r":"SEH-ee","en":"6"},{"t":"sette","r":"SEHT-teh","en":"7"},{"t":"otto","r":"OHT-toh","en":"8"},{"t":"nove","r":"NOH-veh","en":"9"},{"t":"dieci","r":"DYEH-chee","en":"10"},{"t":"undici","r":"OON-dee-chee","en":"11"},{"t":"dodici","r":"DOH-dee-chee","en":"12"},{"t":"tredici","r":"TREH-dee-chee","en":"13"},{"t":"quattordici","r":"kwaht-TOHR-dee-chee","en":"14"},{"t":"quindici","r":"kween-DEE-chee","en":"15"},{"t":"sedici","r":"SEH-dee-chee","en":"16"},{"t":"diciassette","r":"dee-chahs-SEHT-teh","en":"17"},{"t":"diciotto","r":"dee-CHOHT-toh","en":"18"},{"t":"diciannove","r":"dee-chahn-NOH-veh","en":"19"},{"t":"venti","r":"VEHN-tee","en":"20"},{"t":"trenta","r":"TREHN-tah","en":"30"},{"t":"quaranta","r":"kwah-RAHN-tah","en":"40"},{"t":"cinquanta","r":"cheen-KWAHN-tah","en":"50"},{"t":"sessanta","r":"sehs-SAHN-tah","en":"60"},{"t":"settanta","r":"seht-TAHN-tah","en":"70"},{"t":"ottanta","r":"oht-TAHN-tah","en":"80"},{"t":"novanta","r":"noh-VAHN-tah","en":"90"},{"t":"cento","r":"CHEHN-toh","en":"100"}],"rules":["11–16 glue: undici (11), sedici (16). 17–19 double up: diciassette.","21+ drops the vowel: ventuno (21), trentotto (38).","CENTO = 100; DUECENTO = 200."]},"level":{"title":"Beginner: first words, family, food","goals":["Greet people and introduce yourself in Italian","Count, tell age, and talk about family","Order food and use basic present-tense verbs"],"units":[{"id":"A1-U1","title":"First words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U1-L1","title":"Ciao! Greetings and politeness","learn":"CIAO fits friends (hello AND bye!). Strangers get BUONGIORNO (daytime) and BUONASERA (evening). Leaving: ARRIVEDERCI. Magic trio: PER FAVORE (please), GRAZIE (thanks), SCUSI (sorry).","vocab":[{"t":"ciao","r":"chow","en":"hi / bye (friends)","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"buongiorno","r":"bwohn-JOHR-noh","en":"good morning / day","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"buonasera","r":"bwOH-nah-SEH-rah","en":"good evening","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"buonanotte","r":"bwOH-nah-NOHT-teh","en":"good night","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"arrivederci","r":"ahr-ree-veh-DEHR-chee","en":"goodbye","pos":"greeting"},{"t":"per favore","r":"pehr fah-VOH-reh","en":"please","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"grazie","r":"GRAH-tsyeh","en":"thanks","pos":"noun"},{"t":"scusi","r":"SKOO-zee","en":"sorry / excuse me","pos":"verb"}],"grammar":{"title":"Articles: IL/LO/LA + UN/UNO/UNA","explain":"Masculine: IL libro, but LO before s+consonant/z (LO zaino). Feminine: LA casa. A/AN: UN libro, UNO zaino, UNA casa. Learn nouns WITH articles!","pattern":"il/lo + masculine · la + feminine","examples":[{"t":"il libro","r":"eel LEE-broh","en":"the book"},{"t":"la casa","r":"lah KAH-zah","en":"the house"},{"t":"uno zaino","r":"OO-noh DZAH-ee-noh","en":"a backpack"}],"mistakes":["Saying IL zaino — s/z words take LO/UNO: LO zaino.","Saying LA libro — libro is masculine: IL libro."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Buongiorno! Come stai?","r":"bwohn-JOHR-noh! KOH-meh STEH-ee?","en":"Hello! How are you?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Molto bene, grazie. E tu?","r":"MOHL-toh BEH-neh, GRAH-tsyeh. eh too?","en":"Very well, thanks. And you?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Bene, grazie. Arrivederci!","r":"BEH-neh, GRAH-tsyeh. ahr-ree-veh-DEHR-chee!","en":"Fine, thanks. Goodbye!"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Arrivederci!","r":"ahr-ree-veh-DEHR-chee!","en":"Goodbye!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello (to a friend)","answer":"ciao"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: thank you","answer":"grazie"},{"type":"fill","q":"Buon___ (evening)","answer":"asera"},{"type":"choose","q":"Which means 'please'?","options":["grazie","per favore","ciao","scusi"],"answer":"per favore"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Buongiorno, grazie.","answer":"Buongiorno, grazie."}],"quiz":[{"q":"CIAO is used…","options":["only mornings","with friends, hello and bye","only nights","never"],"answer":1,"why":"Ciao = casual hi/bye."},{"q":"BUONASERA is for…","options":["morning","evening","night sleep","lunch"],"answer":1,"why":"Sera = evening."},{"q":"IL LIBRO means…","options":["the house","the book","the coffee","the door"],"answer":1,"why":"Libro (masculine) = book."},{"q":"LO ZAINO uses LO because…","options":["it is feminine","z-words take LO","it is plural","no reason"],"answer":1,"why":"S+consonant/Z take LO."},{"q":"SCUSI means…","options":["please","thanks","sorry","hello"],"answer":2,"why":"Scusi = sorry/excuse me."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Greetings worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Match the greeting to its use.","items":["buongiorno","buonasera","ciao"],"key":["hello (daytime)","good evening","hi/bye (friends)"]},{"instruction":"Fill in: il, lo, or la.","items":["___ casa","___ libro","___ zaino"],"key":["la","il","lo"]},{"instruction":"Write the magic words.","items":["please","thanks","sorry"],"key":["per favore","grazie","scusi"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U1-L2","title":"Numbers and introductions","learn":"Numbers 1–10 open prices and ages. Introduce with ESSERE (to be): SONO = I am. Sono Sofia. Ask names: COME TI CHIAMI? (What are you called?). Answer: MI CHIAMO …","vocab":[{"t":"uno","r":"OO-noh","en":"one","pos":"number"},{"t":"due","r":"DOO-eh","en":"two","pos":"number"},{"t":"tre","r":"treh","en":"three","pos":"number"},{"t":"quattro","r":"KWAHT-troh","en":"four","pos":"number"},{"t":"cinque","r":"CHEEN-kweh","en":"five","pos":"number"},{"t":"sei","r":"SEH-ee","en":"six","pos":"number"},{"t":"sette","r":"SEHT-teh","en":"seven","pos":"number"},{"t":"otto","r":"OHT-toh","en":"eight","pos":"number"},{"t":"nove","r":"NOH-veh","en":"nine","pos":"number"},{"t":"dieci","r":"DYEH-chee","en":"ten","pos":"number"}],"grammar":{"title":"ESSERE: sono, sei, è","explain":"SONO = I am, SEI = you are, È = he/she is. Drop the pronoun: SONO Sofia is enough! È wears an accent (è) — never confuse with E (and)!","pattern":"sono · sei · è","examples":[{"t":"Sono Sofia.","r":"SOH-noh soh-FEE-ah.","en":"I am Sofia."},{"t":"Sei Marco?","r":"SEH-ee MAHR-koh?","en":"Are you Marco?"},{"t":"È italiano.","r":"eh ee-tah-LYAH-noh.","en":"He is Italian."}],"mistakes":["Saying E (and) for È (is) — is needs the accent: È!","Saying IO SONO every time — SONO alone is natural."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Ciao, sono Sofia. Come ti chiami?","r":"chow, SOH-noh soh-FEE-ah. KOH-meh tee KYAH-mee?","en":"Hi, I am Sofia. What is your name?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Mi chiamo Marco. Di dove sei?","r":"mee KYAH-moh MAHR-koh. dee DOH-veh SEH-ee?","en":"My name is Marco. Where are you from?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Sono di Roma.","r":"SOH-noh dee ROH-mah.","en":"I am from Rome."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Piacere!","r":"pyah-CHEH-reh!","en":"Nice to meet you!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Sofia","answer":"Sono Sofia"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ Marco? (are you)","answer":"Sei"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I am' in Italian is…","options":["è","sei","sono","siamo"],"answer":"sono"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: Sofia / sono","answer":"sono Sofia"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Mi chiamo Marco.","answer":"Mi chiamo Marco."}],"quiz":[{"q":"SONO means…","options":["you are","I am","he is","we are"],"answer":1,"why":"Sono = I am."},{"q":"How do you ask someone's name?","options":["Come stai?","Come ti chiami?","Di dove sei?","Quanti anni?"],"answer":1,"why":"Come ti chiami? = What are you called?"},{"q":"CINQUE is number…","options":["3","4","5","6"],"answer":2,"why":"uno due tre quattro CINQUE."},{"q":"'I am from Rome' is…","options":["Sono Roma","Sono di Roma","È di Roma","Sei di Roma"],"answer":1,"why":"Sono DI + place."},{"q":"PIACERE means…","options":["goodbye","nice to meet you","good luck","see you"],"answer":1,"why":"Say it when you first meet."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Numbers and names worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Write the numbers in Italian.","items":["2","5","10"],"key":["due","cinque","dieci"]},{"instruction":"Complete with sono, sei, or è.","items":["___ Sofia (I am)","___ Marco? (are you)","___ italiano (he is)"],"key":["Sono","Sei","È"]},{"instruction":"Introduce yourself in two lines.","items":["Say your name","Say where you are from"],"key":["Sono …","Sono di …"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U2","title":"Daily life","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U2-L1","title":"Family and AVERE (age)","learn":"Meet the family: MADRE, PADRE, FRATELLO, SORELLA. Age uses AVERE (to have): HO 10 ANNI = I have 10 years = I am 10. Ask: QUANTI ANNI HAI? (How many years do you have?)","vocab":[{"t":"la madre","r":"lah MAH-dreh","en":"mother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il padre","r":"eel PAH-dreh","en":"father","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il fratello","r":"eel frah-TEHL-loh","en":"brother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la sorella","r":"lah soh-REHL-lah","en":"sister","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il figlio","r":"eel FEE-lyoh","en":"son","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la figlia","r":"lah FEE-lyah","en":"daughter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la famiglia","r":"lah fah-MEE-lyah","en":"family","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'amico / l'amica","r":"lah-MEE-koh","en":"friend (m/f)","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"AVERE for age: ho… anni","explain":"HO = I have, HAI = you have, HA = he/she has. Age: HO + number + ANNI. QUANTI ANNI HAI? = How old are you? (H is silent: HO = oh!)","pattern":"ho/hai/ha + number + anni","examples":[{"t":"Ho dieci anni.","r":"oh DYEH-chee AHN-nee.","en":"I am 10 years old."},{"t":"Quanti anni hai?","r":"KWAHN-tee AHN-nee EH-ee?","en":"How old are you?"},{"t":"Mia sorella ha sette anni.","r":"MEE-ah soh-REHL-lah ah SEHT-teh AHN-nee.","en":"My sister is 7."}],"mistakes":["Saying SONO dieci anni — age always uses AVERE.","Pronouncing the H in HO — silent! HO = oh."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Hai fratelli?","r":"EH-ee frah-TEHL-lee?","en":"Do you have brothers/sisters?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Sì, ho un fratello e una sorella.","r":"see, oh oon frah-TEHL-loh eh OO-nah soh-REHL-lah.","en":"Yes, I have one brother and one sister."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Quanti anni ha tua sorella?","r":"KWAHN-tee AHN-nee ah TOO-ah soh-REHL-lah?","en":"How old is your sister?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Ha sette anni.","r":"ah SEHT-teh AHN-nee.","en":"She is seven."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am 10 years old","answer":"Ho dieci anni"},{"type":"fill","q":"Mia sorella ___ sette anni. (has)","answer":"ha"},{"type":"choose","q":"'How old are you?' is…","options":["Come stai?","Quanti anni hai?","Come ti chiami?","Di dove sei?"],"answer":"Quanti anni hai?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: anni / ho / dieci","answer":"ho dieci anni"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Ho un fratello.","answer":"Ho un fratello."}],"quiz":[{"q":"HO DIECI ANNI means…","options":["I have ten houses","I am ten years old","I like ten songs","I see ten birds"],"answer":1,"why":"Avere + anni = age."},{"q":"LA SORELLA is…","options":["brother","sister","mother","daughter"],"answer":1,"why":"Sorella = sister."},{"q":"Which asks about age?","options":["Come stai?","Quanti anni hai?","Dove abiti?","Che ore sono?"],"answer":1,"why":"Quanti anni = how many years."},{"q":"'My sister is 7' is…","options":["Mia sorella ha sette anni","Mia sorella è sette","Mia sorella sette anni","Ho sorella sette"],"answer":0,"why":"Ha + number + anni."},{"q":"UN FRATELLO E UNA SORELLA means…","options":["two brothers","two sisters","a brother and a sister","no siblings"],"answer":2,"why":"Un = a (m), una = a (f)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Family worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["mother","brother","family"],"key":["la madre","il fratello","la famiglia"]},{"instruction":"Write the age sentence.","items":["I am 8 (years)","My brother is 5"],"key":["Ho otto anni","Mio fratello ha cinque anni"]},{"instruction":"Answer about yourself.","items":["Hai fratelli?","Quanti anni hai?"],"key":["Sì/No, (ho…)","Ho … anni"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U2-L2","title":"Food and -ARE verbs","learn":"Food first! ACQUA, PANE, LATTE, MELA. Order with VORREI (I would like): VORREI UN CAFFÈ. -ARE verbs: PARLARE → PARLO (I speak), PARLI (you speak), PARLA (he/she speaks).","vocab":[{"t":"l'acqua","r":"LAHK-kwah","en":"water","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il pane","r":"eel PAH-neh","en":"bread","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il latte","r":"eel LAHT-teh","en":"milk","pos":"noun"},{"t":"la mela","r":"lah MEH-lah","en":"apple","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il riso","r":"eel REE-zoh","en":"rice","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il pollo","r":"eel POHL-loh","en":"chicken","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il caffè","r":"eel kahf-FEH","en":"coffee","pos":"noun"},{"t":"il tè","r":"eel teh","en":"tea","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Present -ARE: parlo, parli, parla","explain":"Drop -ARE, add -O (I), -I (you), -A (he/she). PARLARE → parlo, parli, parla. MANGIARE → mangio, mangi, mangia. One pattern, hundreds of verbs!","pattern":"stem + o/i/a","examples":[{"t":"Parlo italiano.","r":"PAHR-loh ee-tah-LYAH-noh.","en":"I speak Italian."},{"t":"Parli inglese?","r":"PAHR-lee een-GLEH-zeh?","en":"Do you speak English?"},{"t":"Lei canta bene.","r":"LEH-ee KAHN-tah BEH-neh.","en":"She sings well."}],"mistakes":["Saying TU PARLA for 'you speak' — you = PARLI.","Keeping -ARE: PARLO, not PARLARO."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"Buongiorno! Vorrei un caffè, per favore.","r":"bwohn-JOHR-noh! vohr-REH-ee oon kahf-FEH, pehr fah-VOH-reh.","en":"Hello! I would like a coffee, please."},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Grande o piccolo?","r":"GRAHN-deh oh PEEK-koh-loh?","en":"Large or small?"},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Grande, grazie. Quanto costa?","r":"GRAHN-deh, GRAH-tsyeh. KWAHN-toh KOH-stah?","en":"Large, thanks. How much is it?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Due euro.","r":"DOO-eh eh-OO-roh.","en":"Two euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I speak Italian","answer":"Parlo italiano"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ inglese? (do YOU speak)","answer":"Parli"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I would like a coffee' starts with…","options":["Voglio","Vorrei","Ho","Sono"],"answer":"Vorrei"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: caffè / vorrei / un","answer":"vorrei un caffè"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Vorrei un tè, per favore.","answer":"Vorrei un tè, per favore."}],"quiz":[{"q":"PARLI means…","options":["I speak","you speak","he speaks","they speak"],"answer":1,"why":"-I = you."},{"q":"IL POLLO is…","options":["bread","rice","chicken","apple"],"answer":2,"why":"Pollo = chicken."},{"q":"QUANTO COSTA? means…","options":["Where is it?","How much is it?","What time is it?","Who is it?"],"answer":1,"why":"Quanto = how much."},{"q":"'She sings well' is…","options":["Lei canto bene","Lei canta bene","Lei canti bene","Lei cantare bene"],"answer":1,"why":"She = -A: canta."},{"q":"The polite order word is…","options":["voglio","vorrei","ho","dammi"],"answer":1,"why":"Vorrei = I would like."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Food worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["water","milk","apple"],"key":["l'acqua","il latte","la mela"]},{"instruction":"Conjugate PARLARE.","items":["I speak","you speak","she speaks"],"key":["parlo","parli","parla"]},{"instruction":"Order politely in a café.","items":["a coffee, please","How much is it?"],"key":["Vorrei un caffè, per favore","Quanto costa?"]}]}}]},{"id":"A1-U3","title":"Describing words","lessons":[{"id":"A1-U3-L1","title":"Colors and adjectives","learn":"Adjectives match gender AND number: -O (m), -A (f), -I (m plural), -E (f plural). IL LIBRO ROSSO, LA CASA ROSSA, I LIBRI ROSSI, LE CASE ROSSE. Position: AFTER the noun!","vocab":[{"t":"rosso","r":"ROHS-soh","en":"red","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"blu","r":"bloo","en":"blue","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"verde","r":"VEHR-deh","en":"green","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"giallo","r":"JAHL-loh","en":"yellow","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"bianco","r":"BYAHN-koh","en":"white","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"nero","r":"NEH-roh","en":"black","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"grande","r":"GRAHN-deh","en":"big","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"piccolo","r":"PEEK-koh-loh","en":"small","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"Four endings: -o/-a/-i/-e","explain":"ROSSO (m), ROSSA (f), ROSSI (m plural), ROSSE (f plural). -E adjectives (verde, grande): VERDE → VERDI (plural both genders). BLU never changes!","pattern":"-o/-a (sing) · -i/-e (plural)","examples":[{"t":"Il libro rosso.","r":"eel LEE-broh ROHS-soh.","en":"The red book."},{"t":"La casa bianca.","r":"lah KAH-zah BYAHN-kah.","en":"The white house."},{"t":"Le scarpe nere.","r":"leh SKAHR-peh NEH-reh.","en":"The black shoes."}],"mistakes":["Saying LA casa BIANCO — feminine needs BIANCA.","Saying I LIBRI ROSSE — masculine plural is ROSSI."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Mi piace la casa bianca.","r":"mee PYAH-cheh lah KAH-zah BYAHN-kah.","en":"I like the white house."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"E la macchina rossa?","r":"eh lah mahk-KEE-nah ROHS-sah?","en":"And the red car?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"È molto bella.","r":"eh MOHL-toh BEHL-lah.","en":"It is very pretty."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Sì, è grande e rossa.","r":"see, eh GRAHN-deh eh ROHS-sah.","en":"Yes, it is big and red."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: the red book","answer":"il libro rosso"},{"type":"fill","q":"La casa ___ (white)","answer":"bianca"},{"type":"choose","q":"'The black shoes' is…","options":["Le scarpe nero","Le scarpe nere","I scarpe neri","La scarpa nera"],"answer":"Le scarpe nere"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: casa / bianca / la","answer":"la casa bianca"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Mi piace la casa bianca.","answer":"Mi piace la casa bianca."}],"quiz":[{"q":"LA CASA BIANCA means…","options":["the white house","the black house","the big house","the red house"],"answer":0,"why":"Casa (f) + bianca."},{"q":"I LIBRI ROSSI: why ROSSI?","options":["it is long","masculine plural -I","books are red","all adjectives"],"answer":1,"why":"Masculine plural: -I."},{"q":"LE SCARPE NERE means…","options":["the black shoe","the black shoes","the white shoes","the red shoes"],"answer":1,"why":"Scarpe (f pl) + nere."},{"q":"BLU in plural is…","options":["blui","blue","blu (never changes)","bli"],"answer":2,"why":"Blu is invariable!"},{"q":"Adjectives usually go…","options":["before the noun","after the noun","at sentence start","nowhere"],"answer":1,"why":"La casa bianca — after!"}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Colors worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["red","blue","small"],"key":["rosso","blu","piccolo"]},{"instruction":"Match the adjective.","items":["il libro ___ (red)","la casa ___ (white)","le scarpe ___ (black)"],"key":["rosso","bianca","nere"]},{"instruction":"Describe two things.","items":["The white house","The red car"],"key":["la casa bianca","la macchina rossa"]}]}},{"id":"A1-U3-L2","title":"Days, months, and telling time","learn":"Days are lowercase except with capitals? No — Italian days are LOWERCASE: lunedì, martedì. Time: CHE ORE SONO? È L'UNA (1:00) but SONO LE TRE (others). Half: E MEZZA.","vocab":[{"t":"lunedì","r":"loo-neh-DEE","en":"Monday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"martedì","r":"mahr-teh-DEE","en":"Tuesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"mercoledì","r":"mehr-koh-leh-DEE","en":"Wednesday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"oggi","r":"OHJ-jee","en":"today","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"domani","r":"doh-MAH-nee","en":"tomorrow","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"ieri","r":"YEH-ree","en":"yesterday","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"la settimana","r":"lah seht-tee-MAH-nah","en":"week","pos":"noun"},{"t":"l'ora","r":"LOH-rah","en":"hour / time","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Telling time: è l'una / sono le…","explain":"È L'UNA (1:00 — singular), SONO LE DUE/TRE… (plural). Half: E MEZZA — SONO LE TRE E MEZZA (3:30). Quarter: E UN QUARTO.","pattern":"è l'una · sono le + number (+ e mezza)","examples":[{"t":"È l'una.","r":"eh LOO-nah.","en":"It is one o'clock."},{"t":"Sono le tre.","r":"SOH-noh leh treh.","en":"It is three o'clock."},{"t":"Sono le tre e mezza.","r":"SOH-noh leh treh eh MEHD-dzah.","en":"It is half past three."}],"mistakes":["Saying SONO L'UNA — one o'clock is È L'UNA.","Capitalising days (Lunedì) — Italian days are lowercase."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Marco","t":"Che ore sono?","r":"keh OH-reh SOH-noh?","en":"What time is it?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Sono le tre e mezza.","r":"SOH-noh leh treh eh MEHD-dzah.","en":"It is half past three."},{"sp":"Marco","t":"Ci vediamo domani?","r":"chee veh-DYAH-moh doh-MAH-nee?","en":"Shall we meet tomorrow?"},{"sp":"Sofia","t":"Sì, martedì alle dieci.","r":"see, mahr-teh-DEE AHL-leh DYEH-chee.","en":"Yes, Tuesday at ten."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It is three o'clock","answer":"Sono le tre"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ l'una. (It is)","answer":"È"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Half past three' is…","options":["Sono le tre","Sono le tre e mezza","È le tre","Sono la tre e mezza"],"answer":"Sono le tre e mezza"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: sono / ore / che","answer":"che ore sono"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Sono le tre e mezza.","answer":"Sono le tre e mezza."}],"quiz":[{"q":"È L'UNA is used because…","options":["one is lucky","una is singular","it is morning","all times use È"],"answer":1,"why":"1:00 is singular: È L'."},{"q":"CHE ORE SONO? means…","options":["What day is it?","What time is it?","Where are you?","How are you?"],"answer":1,"why":"Ore = hours/time."},{"q":"E MEZZA means…","options":["and a quarter","and a half","and ten","o'clock sharp"],"answer":1,"why":"Mezza = half."},{"q":"Italian days are written…","options":["CAPITALISED","lowercase","in English","never"],"answer":1,"why":"lunedì, martedì — lowercase."},{"q":"DOMANI means…","options":["today","tomorrow","yesterday","morning"],"answer":1,"why":"Domani = tomorrow."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Time worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Italian.","items":["Monday","today","week"],"key":["lunedì","oggi","la settimana"]},{"instruction":"Write the time.","items":["1:00","3:00","3:30"],"key":["È l'una","Sono le tre","Sono le tre e mezza"]},{"instruction":"Make a plan.","items":["Shall we meet tomorrow?","Yes, Tuesday at ten"],"key":["Ci vediamo domani?","Sì, martedì alle dieci"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: hello (to a friend)","answer":"ciao"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am Sofia","answer":"Sono Sofia"},{"type":"fill","q":"Ho ___ anni (I am 9)","answer":"nove"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Do you speak English?'","options":["Parli inglese?","Parlo inglese?","Parla inglese?","Parlare inglese?"],"answer":"Parli inglese?"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Quanto costa?","answer":"How much is it?"},{"type":"fill","q":"La casa ___ (white)","answer":"bianca"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: anni / ho / dieci","answer":"ho dieci anni"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Vorrei un caffè, per favore.","answer":"Vorrei un caffè, per favore."},{"type":"fill","q":"Sono le tre e ___ (half)","answer":"mezza"},{"type":"choose","q":"'My sister is 7'","options":["Mia sorella ha sette anni","Mia sorella è sette","Mia sorella sette anni","Ho sorella sette"],"answer":"Mia sorella ha sette anni"}]}}}